{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Gives Birth (3rd)","html":"<article id='sn1.57'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 1.57 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 1.57 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>6. Jarāvagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>6. Old Age </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Tatiyajanasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Gives Birth (3rd) </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Kiṁsu janeti purisaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“What gives birth to a person? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kiṁsu tassa vidhāvati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What do they have that runs about? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kiṁsu saṁsāramāpādi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What enters transmigration? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kiṁsu tassa parāyanan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What is their destiny?” </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Taṇhā janeti purisaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Craving gives birth to a person. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>cittamassa vidhāvati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Their mind is what runs about. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Satto saṁsāramāpādi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A sentient being enters transmigration. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kammaṁ tassa parāyanan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Deeds are their final haven.” </span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
